{"units": [{"id": "ō-note5", "translation": "Vocatives placed without ὦ in exclamatory or address formulas, although among the scenic poets examples are much fewer than those with added ὦ, yet not rarely the vocative is placed even without ὦ, as the examples cited under the individual words show: see ἄναξ, γυνή, δεσπότης, θυγάτηρ, μήτηρ, ξένος, παῖς, πατήρ, τέκνον. But whoever wishes to inspect these examples and those of the other scenic poets will easily notice that in most cases ὦ has been omitted solely on account of metrical necessity, especially in the even positions of senarii. Yet it is not improbable that the poets sometimes had other reasons besides meter for adding or omitting ὦ, about which I have spoken in the Lexicon Sophocleum p. 525, citing the example from Euripides' Andromeda ὦ θεοὶ, τίν᾽ ἐς γῆν βαρβάρων ἀφίγμεθα; [O gods, to what land of barbarians have we come?] where Euripides well perceived that ὦ θεοί [O gods], to be pronounced with synizesis at the beginning of the speech, is more fitting and weightier than the light iambus θεοί [gods] without ὦ."}, {"id": "ō-quote1", "translation": "O gods, of a trusty helper."}, {"id": "ō-quote2", "translation": "O gods, indeed – we have encountered."}, {"id": "ō-quote3", "translation": "O wretched one, what a youth of allies he has destroyed."}, {"id": "ō-quote4", "translation": "O divine power, how many evils come upon me."}, {"id": "ō-quote5", "translation": "A grievous suffering, O gods, an unbearable evil."}, {"id": "ō-quote6", "translation": "O ungrateful one, for the many kisses."}, {"id": "ō-quote7", "translation": "O hail, lamp of night."}, {"id": "ō-quote8", "translation": "O hail, old man."}, {"id": "ō-quote9", "translation": "Raise a cry, O you who have escaped the evils of the master's house."}, {"id": "ō-quote10", "translation": "896 O child."}, {"id": "ō-quote11", "translation": "You have met with a bitter suitor, O maiden."}, {"id": "ō-quote12", "translation": "O maidens."}, {"id": "ō-quote13", "translation": "Dare, O foolish one."}, {"id": "ō-quote14", "translation": "O Zeus and Earth;"}, {"id": "ō-quote15", "translation": "O father Zeus."}, {"id": "ō-quote16", "translation": "O consummation."}, {"id": "ō-quote17", "translation": "409 788. Suppl. 209 O Zeus."}, {"id": "ō-quote18", "translation": "Be silent, O wretched one."}, {"id": "ō-quote19", "translation": "853. Ch. 100 O dear ones."}, {"id": "ō-quote20", "translation": "O wretched ones,"}, {"id": "ō-quote21", "translation": "O queen of the deep-girdled Persians, most exalted."}, {"id": "ō-quote22", "translation": "619 O friends."}, {"id": "ō-quote23", "translation": "O mistress."}, {"id": "ō-quote24", "translation": "O children of the Greeks."}, {"id": "ō-quote25", "translation": "O king Zeus."}, {"id": "ō-quote26", "translation": "1247 O wretched one."}, {"id": "ō-quote27", "translation": "O woman much wretched, and much wise."}, {"id": "ō-quote28", "translation": "O enduring one."}, {"id": "ō-quote29", "translation": "1407 O woman."}, {"id": "ō-quote30", "translation": "O master."}, {"id": "ō-quote31", "translation": "O children."}, {"id": "ō-quote32", "translation": "910 922 O child."}, {"id": "ō-quote33", "translation": "O father."}, {"id": "ō-quote34", "translation": "O earth."}, {"id": "ō-quote35", "translation": "O Persephassa."}, {"id": "ō-quote36", "translation": "O stranger."}, {"id": "ō-quote37", "translation": "O strangers."}, {"id": "ō-quote38", "translation": "O goddesses beneath the earth."}, {"id": "ō-quote39", "translation": "O mother Night."}, {"id": "ō-quote40", "translation": "O murderer."}, {"id": "ō-quote41", "translation": "O Phoebus Apollo."}, {"id": "ō-quote42", "translation": "901 O king, child of Earth, Zeus."}, {"id": "ō-quote43", "translation": "O children."}, {"id": "ō-quote44", "translation": "O foot, I will release you."}, {"id": "ō-quote45", "translation": "Who is within, O child, child?"}, {"id": "ō-quote46", "translation": "O lord."}, {"id": "ō-quote47", "translation": "1077 O Apollo, O Apollo,"}, {"id": "ō-quote48", "translation": "O divine aether."}, {"id": "ō-quote49", "translation": "O greatly blessed maiden."}, {"id": "ō-quote50", "translation": "O revered Fates."}, {"id": "ō-quote51", "translation": "O Zeus-born, war-loving might."}, {"id": "ō-quote52", "translation": "O dearest daughter of Leto."}, {"id": "ō-quote53", "translation": "O dear Apollo."}, {"id": "ō-quote54", "translation": "O dear child of Oedipus."}, {"id": "ō-quote55", "translation": "O all-powerful Zeus."}, {"id": "ō-quote56", "translation": "O city-protecting gods."}, {"id": "ō-quote57", "translation": "O great Zeus."}, {"id": "ō-quote58", "translation": "O black – curse."}, {"id": "ō-quote59", "translation": "O greatly boasting – Furies."}, {"id": "ō-quote60", "translation": "O greatest hate."}, {"id": "ō-quote61", "translation": "O hateful divine power."}, {"id": "ō-quote62", "translation": "O toil-bringing divine power."}, {"id": "ō-quote63", "translation": "O faithful companions of faithful ones and of my youth."}, {"id": "ō-quote64", "translation": "O aged mother of Xerxes."}, {"id": "ō-quote65", "translation": "O dearest of men."}, {"id": "ō-quote66", "translation": "O dearest object of care."}, {"id": "ō-quote67", "translation": "O delightful sight."}, {"id": "ō-quote68", "translation": "O great Fates."}, {"id": "ō-quote69", "translation": "O hard-to-wrestle curse."}, {"id": "ō-quote70", "translation": "O revered earth."}, {"id": "ō-quote71", "translation": "O wretched me."}, {"id": "ō-quote72", "translation": "O all-hated monsters."}, {"id": "ō-quote73", "translation": "O new toils of the house."}, {"id": "ō-quote74", "translation": "O visible vision of night."}, {"id": "ō-quote75", "translation": "O kindly light."}, {"id": "ō-quote76", "translation": "O father who suffered terribly."}, {"id": "ō-quote77", "translation": "O inborn toil."}, {"id": "ō-quote78", "translation": "O black Night."}, {"id": "ō-quote79", "translation": "O much-hated handicraft."}, {"id": "ō-quote80", "translation": "O common benefit appearing to mortals."}, {"id": "ō-quote81", "translation": "O much-lamented dead ruler."}, {"id": "ō-quote82", "translation": "O you who surpass all mortals."}, {"id": "ō-quote83", "translation": "O you who dwell in the great mouth."}, {"id": "ō-quote84", "translation": "O you who hold all power over the earth."}]}